    <item rdf:about="https://www.resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agentic_framework:insolvency_agents&amp;rev=1745254236&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-21T16:50:36+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>insolvency_agents</title>
        <link>https://www.resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agentic_framework:insolvency_agents&amp;rev=1745254236&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Insolvency Agents

AI agents can be categorized into distinct groups based on their roles and functionalities, offering specialized capabilities to enhance efficiency, accuracy, and decision-making in insolvency processes. These categories include Legal Agents, Process Agents, Planning Agents, Marketing Agents, Fraud Detection Agents, and Prediction Agents. Each type of agent addresses specific challenges within the insolvency framework, streamlining operations and improving outcomes.</description>
    </item>
